WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.520
Authorization may depend on a database,
role directory, entitlement store,

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.187
license service, policy engine, or
centralized authorization API.

3
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.606
Those dependencies improve consistency but
add failure modes.

4
00:00:11.686 --> 00:00:15.520
A timeout, connection error, invalid
response, circuit-breaker state,

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.806
or unexpected exception is an availability
problem and an indeterminate policy

6
00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.566
evaluation.

7
00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:23.058
It is never positive authorization
evidence.

8
00:00:23.138 --> 00:00:26.972
Set deadlines shorter than the overall
request budget and limit retries.

9
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:30.083
Retrying can improve resilience for
transient failures,

10
00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.698
but exhaustion must return a non-grant
outcome.

11
00:00:32.778 --> 00:00:36.983
A circuit breaker should fail quickly into
indeterminate, not bypass the check.

12
00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:39.785
Validate remote responses before accepting
allow,

13
00:00:39.865 --> 00:00:42.338
and bind a response to the request it
evaluated.

14
00:00:42.418 --> 00:00:46.809
Broad catch blocks should translate known
failures while preserving an observable

15
00:00:46.889 --> 00:00:50.662
cause; they must not return true or fall
through to the protected branch.

16
00:00:50.742 --> 00:00:53.092
Place evaluation before irreversible work;

17
00:00:53.172 --> 00:00:57.748
compensating actions and transaction
rollback are not substitutes when external side

18
00:00:57.828 --> 00:00:59.621
effects cannot be fully reversed.

19
00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:04.030
Do not hide infrastructure failure by
converting every exception into an ordinary

20
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.450
deny when operations teams need to
distinguish the conditions.

21
00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.200
Both outcomes block the action,

22
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.856
but denial indicates a successful policy
decision while indeterminate indicates that

23
00:01:13.936 --> 00:01:16.224
the application could not decide reliably.

24
00:01:16.304 --> 00:01:20.138
That distinction supports accurate alerts,
service-level objectives,

25
00:01:20.218 --> 00:01:22.321
retry guidance, and incident response.

26
00:01:22.401 --> 00:01:25.060
Expose only sanitized details to clients
and logs.

27
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.542
Choose the user-visible response according
to the API contract.

28
00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:31.095
A real denial may use forbidden,
unauthorized,

29
00:01:31.175 --> 00:01:34.886
or not found depending on authentication
state and disclosure policy.

30
00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:38.862
A policy dependency outage may use service
unavailable, gateway timeout,

31
00:01:38.942 --> 00:01:39.932
or internal error.

32
00:01:40.012 --> 00:01:43.042
Response-code secrecy is not the
authorization control.

33
00:01:43.122 --> 00:01:46.709
The control is structural: no database
mutation, message emission,

34
00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:51.056
file operation, or privileged downstream
call occurs until an explicit allow has

35
00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:51.940
been accepted.
